++From 34003e8b6a4772ec50db5525ccd8017bddca7816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
++Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 20:52:55 +0000
++Subject: [PATCH 01/17] Restore lost PP+CP fixes and add float8 dtype guards
++
++Recovered sparse_mla_attention.py and modeling_glm_moe_dsa.py from the
++2026-08-02 snapshot after they were overwritten with the Docker image's
++stock copies, restoring _FiniteGrad gradient sanitization and PRESCALE_QK.
++
++The snapshot predates two fixes that the clobbered files evidently carried,
++re-derived here from the crash:
++
++* _context_parallel_state used self.layers[0]. Under pipeline parallelism
++  apply_pp_boundaries swaps the ModuleList for an nn.ModuleDict keyed by
++  global layer index as a string, so this raised KeyError: 0.
++* The forward loop sliced self.layers and used enumerate(), which cannot
++  work on a ModuleDict and would have handed routed_experts a local 0-based
++  index instead of the global one, replaying the wrong layer's router on
++  every stage after the first.
++
++Also guards the float8 promotion errors that surface only under
++quantization.dequantize_checkpoint = false, where FSDP applies a bare
++MixedPrecisionPolicy() and nothing normalizes activation dtypes.
