++Subject: [PATCH 07/17] Revert trainer to bf16 weights: fp8 compute broke the
++ importance ratio
++
++x19 metrics over 5 steps:
++  masked_advantage_positive/mean  0.003 0.004 0.000 0.004 0.002
++  masked_advantage_negative/mean  0.637 0.690 0.639 0.670 0.759
++  masked_mismatch_kl/mean         7.09  7.75  7.13  7.52  8.58
++
++mismatch_kl of 7-9 nats means the trainer's logprobs differ from the ones
++vLLM sampled with by an importance ratio around e^3. The DPPO trust region
++then masks anything that far out, and it masked essentially every
++positive-advantage token -- leaving pure negative signal. That is why entropy
++rose monotonically (9.155 -> 9.200) while reward fell (0.130 -> 0.093).
++
++A single fp8 linear measures 2.56% relative error against its bf16
++equivalent; compounded over 78 layers the trainer's distribution no longer
++resembles the sampler's. Entropy of 9.2 nats against a vocab ceiling of 11.95
++is far flatter than a trained policy should be.
++
++fp8 trainer weights only ever existed to dodge the host memory ceiling, and
++ac_offloading turned out to be the real cause of that (79815a3). With
++offloading off, host memory sat at 3 GB against 460 GB free, so bf16 weights
++fit. Also back to pp=8 now that n76 has recovered.
