++From fec05bf0d35fcb06769a0be502bdce440c839c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
++Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:17:27 +0000
++Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Watchdog: always rebuild tunnels, never refuse on mass
++ failure
++
++The >=80%-failure refusal I added earlier froze the run for five hours. At
++batch 1024 all 24 tunnels wedged at once under 4x the rollout load while the
++engines were healthy and generating; the guard read that as a dead backend and
++sat idle. 198 rollout failures per 5 min, all ReadTimeout against dead
++tunnels.
++
++The failure modes are not symmetric: rebuilding against a dead backend costs
++nothing (it fails again next cycle), refusing to rebuild against a live one
++halts everything. Warn on mass failure, rebuild regardless.
++
++Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
++Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
