@@ -0,0 +1,281 @@
+From a2cd8f6c75aacd1e43633de04a4d408169ba788a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 03:44:15 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 19/19] Deslop the handoff docs per slop-guard categories
+
+Checked against the slop-guard ruleset. The STE constraint had already removed
+the structural categories: no em dashes, no mid-sentence bold, no bullets, no
+blockquotes, no horizontal rules, no long sentences.
+
+Three categories needed work:
+
+Repeated 4-8 word phrases. "The rule:" opened 9 paragraphs and "The fix:"
+opened 5. Both are now varied imperatives.
+
+Aphoristic closers. Removed "This rule has no exception", "A fast rollout that
+the trainer never receives has no value", and the "costs nothing / stops the
+run" contrast pair. Replaced with plain statements of consequence.
+
+Copula chains. Broke the back-to-back "The X is / The Y are" pairs. Left the
+single declaratives, which ASD-STE100 requires.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
+---
+ docs/CHANGES.md | 12 +++++-----
+ docs/HANDOFF.md | 63 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------------
+ 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/docs/CHANGES.md b/docs/CHANGES.md
+index 709e86f..f0dc0dd 100644
+--- a/docs/CHANGES.md
++++ b/docs/CHANGES.md
+@@ -34,22 +34,22 @@ File: `configs/china/trainer.x*.toml`
+ Activation offloading was on by default. It put activations into pinned host
+ memory. The host memory then reached 486 GB of 503 GB. The nodes stopped.
+ 
+-This change is the reason that a 16K step is possible.
++Without this change a 16K step does not complete.
+ 
+ # train.py: the stage buffer dtype
+ 
+ The inter-stage buffers hold activations. The code took the dtype from the
+ first parameter. With FP8 weights the first parameter is `float8_e4m3fn`.
+ 
+-The fix uses `DTYPE_MAP[config.model.optimization_dtype]`.
++Use `DTYPE_MAP[config.model.optimization_dtype]` instead.
+ 
+ # train.py: discard a corrupt batch
+ 
+ A micro-batch arrived with the shape `[1, 9142729177965406720]`. Torch stopped
+ rank 0. The other 7 ranks waited for the NCCL timeout.
+ 
+-The fix tests each micro-batch shape. The limit is `seq_len * cp * 4`. A bad
+-batch is discarded. The run continues.
++The code now tests each micro-batch shape against `seq_len * cp * 4`. It
++discards a bad batch and the run continues.
+ 
+ # modeling_glm_moe_dsa.py: the ModuleDict layers
+ 
+@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ A widening from float8 to bf16 is exact. `bitcast` is always false in
+ float8 on the main path. The tensors `cos` and `sin` are float8 through
+ `compute_sparse_indices`.
+ 
+-The fix makes all three tensors a real float type. Rope must not use float8.
++The code now makes all three tensors a real float type. Rope must not use float8.
+ The e4m3 format has 3 mantissa bits. That is not sufficient for the phase.
+ 
+ # norms.py: the float8 guards
+@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@ The new cost is `layers * (weights + activations * in_flight)`.
+ Do not use only the activations. That objective gives 32 of 78 layers to the
+ last stage. The weights then need 52 GB on a 48 GB card.
+ 
+-The result: the peak changed from 24.6 GB to 21.9 GB for each GPU.
++The peak changed from 24.6 GB to 21.9 GB for each GPU.
+ 
+ # THE NEW SCRIPTS
+ 
+diff --git a/docs/HANDOFF.md b/docs/HANDOFF.md
+index 6ae6f39..622a928 100644
+--- a/docs/HANDOFF.md
++++ b/docs/HANDOFF.md
+@@ -21,15 +21,15 @@ The inference engines make the rollouts. They run on 2 hosts. Each host has 8
+ H200 GPUs. The hosts are h200a and h200b. The total is 16 GPUs.
+ 
+ The judge scores the rollouts. It runs on one external host with 8 RTX 5090
+-GPUs. The address is 202.214.223.66 port 26406.
++GPUs. It answers at 202.214.223.66 port 26406.
+ 
+ The orchestrator controls the run. It runs on n82.
+ 
+ # WHAT THE NETWORK IS
+ 
+-The trainer nodes are in China. The engines and the judge are not in China.
+-The link between them is bad. The link loses 10 to 33 percent of the packets.
+-The round trip time is 217 milliseconds.
++The trainer nodes sit in China. The engines and the judge sit outside China.
++The link between them drops 10 to 33 percent of the packets. It adds 217
++milliseconds of round trip time.
+ 
+ The engines connect to n82 with 24 SSH reverse tunnels. The ports are 18001 to
+ 18024.
+@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ The commands are in `docs/RUNBOOK.md`.
+ 
+ # THE RULES THAT THE OWNER GAVE
+ 
+-Do not touch n79. This rule has no exception.
++Do not touch n79.
+ 
+ Do not delete the data of the owner. The protected paths are `/data/ZiphuAI`,
+ `/data/trinity`, and `/data/nv-community_GLM-5.2-NVFP4`. The model at
+@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ those changes. The local changes were lost.
+ The lost code included `_FiniteGrad`. That function removes NaN values from
+ the gradients. The lost code also included `PRESCALE_QK`.
+ 
+-The rule: `scripts/china/cluster.sh` shows which files are mounted into the
++Read `scripts/china/cluster.sh` before you edit these paths. That file shows which files are mounted into the
+ container. Those files have local changes. Do not copy those paths out of the
+ image. Edit the repository copy.
+ 
+@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ The assistant said that the host memory was not real. The assistant called it
+ phantom memory. That diagnosis was wrong. The document `PHANTOM_RAM_PROOF.md`
+ is retracted. The memory was real.
+ 
+-The rule: do not present a theory as a fact. Measure first.
++Measure before you write a conclusion. Do not present a theory as a fact.
+ 
+ # The assistant used a broken health test
+ 
+@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ The assistant used `pgrep -fc <name>` to test if a process runs. That command
+ counts the grep process. The result is always 1 or more. The test always
+ passed. The tunnel watchdog was dead for 3 hours.
+ 
+-The rule: use `pgrep -f "<full command>" | wc -l`. Also read the log file. A
++Use `pgrep -f "<full command>" | wc -l` instead. Also read the log file. A
+ process that runs but does not write to its log does not work.
+ 
+ # The assistant used a watchdog that hid a fault
+@@ -115,8 +115,9 @@ percent of the tunnels fail, do not rebuild them. The reason was to show a
+ dead engine. The rule was wrong. At batch 1024 all 24 tunnels failed at the
+ same time. The engines were healthy. The watchdog did nothing for 5 hours.
+ 
+-The rule: always rebuild the tunnels. A rebuild against a dead engine costs
+-nothing. A refusal against a live engine stops the run.
++Always rebuild the tunnels. A rebuild against a dead engine fails again on the
++next cycle. A refusal to rebuild against a live engine stops the run until an
++operator finds it.
+ 
+ # The assistant tested the engine with the wrong probe
+ 
+@@ -125,7 +126,7 @@ the API server is alive. The EngineCore can be dead when the API server is
+ alive. On 2026-08-06 h200a gave HTTP 200 on `/v1/models`. The same host gave
+ no answer to a completion. The GPU showed 64 requests and 0 tokens per second.
+ 
+-The rule: test the engine with a real completion. Use 3 tokens. Only a
++Test the engine with a real completion. Use 3 tokens. Only a
+ completion proves that the engine works.
+ 
+ # The assistant broke the run with a tunnel restart
+@@ -134,7 +135,7 @@ The assistant killed the batch tunnel while the orchestrator was alive. The
+ zmq session broke. Seven dead connections stayed on port 29620. The batches
+ did not arrive. The trainer waited 27 minutes.
+ 
+-The rule: stop the orchestrator before you touch the batch tunnel.
++Stop the orchestrator before you touch the batch tunnel.
+ 
+ # The assistant deadlocked the start sequence
+ 
+@@ -142,7 +143,7 @@ The assistant made the orchestrator wait for the trainer to bind port 29620.
+ The trainer cannot start until the orchestrator writes `control/orch.toml`.
+ Both parts waited. Nothing happened.
+ 
+-The rule: start the orchestrator first. The trainer starts after it.
++Start the orchestrator first. The trainer starts after it.
+ 
+ # The assistant reported a trend that was noise
+ 
+@@ -151,8 +152,8 @@ used 25 steps. At 36 steps the increase was 6.3 percent. The standard
+ deviation was 0.039. The total trend was 0.013. The trend was inside the
+ noise.
+ 
+-The rule: compare the trend against the standard deviation. Do not report a
+-percentage from a half window.
++Compare the trend against the standard deviation. Do not report a percentage
++from a half window.
+ 
+ # THE FAULTS THAT WERE FOUND IN THE SOFTWARE
+ 
+@@ -169,7 +170,7 @@ the GPU memory.
+ This fault stopped every 16K run for one week. The host memory reached 486 GB
+ of 503 GB. The nodes stopped.
+ 
+-The fix: set `ac_offloading = "None"`.
++Set `ac_offloading = "None"`.
+ 
+ This fault also explains two failed experiments. FP8 weights cut the GPU
+ memory by half. The host memory did not change. `expandable_segments` cut the
+@@ -187,8 +188,8 @@ The adapter server runs on n82 port 8100. The URL used port 18100. Nothing
+ answered on port 18100. Each download failed. Each failed download killed a
+ worker. Each dead worker killed the EngineCore.
+ 
+-The fix: port 18100 forwards to n82 port 8100 on all three hosts. One URL then
+-works everywhere.
++Port 18100 now forwards to n82 port 8100 on all three hosts. One URL then works
++on every host.
+ 
+ Before this fix no run could learn. The engines never received new weights.
+ All rollouts came from the base model. All reward data before run x22 is not
+@@ -205,8 +206,8 @@ The trainer was therefore less exact than the engines. The mismatch KL reached
+ 7 to 9 nats. The trust region then masked almost every positive advantage. The
+ entropy increased to 9.2 nats. The reward decreased.
+ 
+-The fix: `dequantize_checkpoint = true`. The trainer then uses bf16 weights.
+-The mismatch KL decreased to 0.2.
++Set `dequantize_checkpoint = true`. The trainer then uses bf16 weights. The
++mismatch KL decreased to 0.2.
+ 
+ A better fix is possible. Make the trainer use W8A16. The function
+ `_dequant_weight` in `fp8_ada.py` is the start point.
+@@ -218,7 +219,7 @@ Those buffers hold activations. With bf16 weights the two dtypes are the same.
+ With FP8 weights the first parameter is `float8_e4m3fn`. Every hidden-state
+ buffer was then declared FP8.
+ 
+-The fix: use `DTYPE_MAP[config.model.optimization_dtype]`.
++Use `DTYPE_MAP[config.model.optimization_dtype]`.
+ 
+ Do not scan for the first real float parameter. An fp32 `weight_scale_inv` can
+ come before the bf16 weights.
+@@ -251,8 +252,8 @@ On 2026-08-06 a micro-batch arrived with an `input_ids` shape of
+ Torch raised "Storage size calculation overflowed". Rank 0 stopped. The other
+ 7 ranks waited for the NCCL timeout. The run was dead for 6 hours.
+ 
+-The fix: `train.py` now tests each micro-batch shape. A bad batch is
+-discarded. The run continues.
++`train.py` now tests each micro-batch shape. It discards a bad batch and the
++run continues.
+ 
+ # THE LIMITS OF THE SYSTEM
+ 
+@@ -268,8 +269,8 @@ fell to 1 to 6 concurrent requests.
+ At 256 rollouts in flight 20 of 24 tunnels stay healthy. The watchdog rebuilds
+ 1 tunnel each cycle. The engines run 45 to 70 concurrent requests.
+ 
+-The rule: set `batch_size` for the gradient quality. Set
+-`max_inflight_rollouts` to 256. These two values are independent.
++Set `batch_size` for the gradient quality. Set `max_inflight_rollouts` to 256.
++These two values are independent.
+ 
+ # The batch transport cannot cross the link
+ 
+@@ -280,13 +281,13 @@ The orchestrator must run on n82. The batch then goes over the loopback
+ interface. The measured load time is 0.45 seconds.
+ 
+ The cost is that the rollout traffic then crosses the bad link. The rollout
+-collection is slower. This cost is correct. A fast rollout that the trainer
+-never receives has no value.
++collection is slower. Accept this cost. The trainer cannot use a rollout that
++does not arrive.
+ 
+ # The reward is multiplicative
+ 
+-The reward is a product. The factors are the judge score, the coherency, the
+-reasoning, the markdown, and the word count. One factor near zero makes the
++The reward multiplies five factors together: the judge score, the coherency,
++the reasoning, the markdown, and the word count. One factor near zero makes the
+ whole reward near zero.
+ 
+ The 10th percentile of the reward stays near zero. The 90th percentile
+@@ -294,8 +295,8 @@ increased from 0.276 to 0.648. The headroom is at the bottom, not the top.
+ 
+ # THE STATE AT HANDOFF
+ 
+-The run is x24. The configuration is batch 1024, group size 16, 256 rollouts
+-in flight, 16K context, bf16 trainer weights, pipeline parallel 8.
++Run x24 uses batch 1024, group size 16, 256 rollouts in flight, 16K context,
++bf16 trainer weights, and pipeline parallel 8.
+ 
+ Three steps are complete. The step time is 29 to 96 minutes and decreases. The
+ error rate is 42.5, then 27.4, then 13.7 percent. The error rate decreases
+-- 
